Got it. Clean slate. Run these one at a time.

## Step 1: Make sure no Odoo is running

```bash
lsof -ti:8070 | xargs kill -9 2>/dev/null
```

## Step 2: Go to custom folder

```bash
cd ~/Projects/Bytedance/custom
```

## Step 3: Discard ALL current changes (Copilot's edits, your edits, everything)

```bash
git restore .
```

## Step 4: Switch to safe sandbox branch

```bash
git checkout Sandbox-19
```

## Step 5: Delete the feature branch locally

```bash
git branch -D feature/fix-mfg-required-helpdesk
```

## Step 6: Delete it on GitHub too (if it was ever pushed)

```bash
git push origin --delete feature/fix-mfg-required-helpdesk 2>/dev/null
```

(If it says "remote ref does not exist" → fine, means it was never pushed)

## Step 7: Pull latest sandbox

```bash
git pull origin Sandbox-19
```

## Step 8: Verify clean state

```bash
git status
git branch --show-current
```

Expected:
```
nothing to commit, working tree clean
Sandbox-19
```

## Reply

Paste output of Step 8. If both lines look right, you're fully clean and ready for a new task.
